    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d761">

                <pb facs="0877" n="1711" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/1886</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-16T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 16, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1681. For Chadbourne [from War Trade Board]:<anchor n="1" xml:id="d761-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>No. 313. Referring Embassy’s 1886, October 3, 7 p.m., your 303,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d761-f2"/> and Department’s 1610, September 27, 5 p.m., our
                        282,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d761-f3"/> and previous cables<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d761-f4"/> concerning the purchase of mules by A[merican]
                    E[xpeditionary] F[orces]. The War Department has agreed to make available out of
                    its stocks, 20,000 tons of sulphate of ammonia for the purpose of securing
                    release of 50,000 mules. You are authorized to assure the Spanish authorities
                    that the United States will permit the exportation to Spain of 20,000 tons of
                    sulphate of ammonia at the rate of 3,000 tons a month beginning in October, if
                    the Spanish Government will permit the immediate release for the A.E.F. of
                    50,000 mules.</p>
                <p>If this arrangement is made, it is our intention that the licenses for the
                    sulphate of ammonia shall be allocated in accordance with a plan approved by our
                    representative in Spain.</p>
                <p>We are repeating this cablegram to Paris in our No. 385 to McFadden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
